-- title:
--   Inertia-cyclotomic p-torsion classes lie in the finite part
-- statement:
--   Fix an odd prime $p$ and a level $M$ with $p \mid M$, a subgroup $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/M)^{\times}$, and a valuation subring $Pl$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $p$ a non-unit of $Pl$, whose residue field is algebraically closed of characteristic $p$. Given the hypothesis $hj$ that the $q$-expansion of $j$ lies in the $q$-expansion function field of $SL(2,\mathbb{Z})$, a two-chart integral model $\mathfrak{X}$ of $X_H(M)$ over $R_p$, level data $\Lambda$ at $Pl$ and a Néron object $O$ for $J_H(M)$ at $Pl$ over $\Lambda$, together with the hypothesis that the relative sub-Picard problem for $\mathfrak{X}$ cut out by fibrewise algebraic equivalence to zero is represented by the designation formed from $O.G$, $O.g$ and the zero section of the group law $O.L$. Assume the inertia clause: for every $m > 0$, every $\sigma$ in the inertia subgroup of $Pl$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ and every $m$-torsion class $x$ of $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ of the function field of $X_H(M)$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, the difference $\sigma \cdot x - x$ lies in $O.\mathrm{finPts}\,m$, the subgroup generated by the $m$-torsion classes whose associated point over the generic point extends to a point over $\mathrm{Spec}\,Pl$. Then any $p$-torsion class $x$ such that $\sigma \cdot x = c \cdot x$ whenever $\sigma$ lies in that inertia subgroup and acts on the $p$-th roots of unity by $\zeta \mapsto \zeta^{c}$, lies in $O.\mathrm{finPts}\,p$.
--
--   This is the finite-part clause for $p$-torsion on the Jacobian of $X_H(M)$ at a place above $p$: a $p$-torsion class on which inertia acts through the mod $p$ cyclotomic character is captured by the finite part of the Néron object. It feeds the characterisation of the multiplicative-type part of $J_H(M)[p]$ at $p$ and the construction of the homomorphism from $p$-torsion to polar differentials in the ordinary case.
-- source:
